I got you, Ferrier.

725
01:00:49,730 --> 01:00:51,481
- Oh, Jesus.
- You okay?

726
01:00:51,565 --> 01:00:52,607
- Yeah.
- Come on. Come.

727
01:00:52,691 --> 01:00:55,235
- Okay. Jesus. Oh, my God.
- Come on. Come on.

728
01:00:55,569 --> 01:00:57,237
Watch out.

729
01:01:04,495 --> 01:01:05,578
Come on.

730
01:01:06,247 --> 01:01:08,540
- Move. Move. Move.
- Ray.

731
01:01:08,624 --> 01:01:10,458
Ray!

732
01:01:11,502 --> 01:01:13,753
- Come on. Come on. Come on.
- Move it! Get out of here!

733
01:01:15,214 --> 01:01:17,382
Go. I can go with him.

734
01:01:17,466 --> 01:01:18,967
Sheryl?

735
01:01:19,051 --> 01:01:21,302
- Stay back.
- Go with them. Go.

736
01:01:21,387 --> 01:01:22,470
- Ray.
- Sheryl?

737
01:01:22,555 --> 01:01:24,305
- Everybody...
- Sheryl?

738
01:01:24,390 --> 01:01:27,183
- There's room on the boat.
- Let us through, God damn it.

739
01:01:27,268 --> 01:01:29,352
- There's still room on the boat.
- She's a child.

740
01:01:29,436 --> 01:01:31,145
- Robbie.
- There's room on the...

741
01:01:31,230 --> 01:01:33,439
There's still room on the boat.
There's room on the boat.

742
01:01:33,524 --> 01:01:34,566
Up there!

743
01:01:39,613 --> 01:01:41,406
- Robbie.
- Just stay with me.

744
01:01:41,490 --> 01:01:43,533
Stay with me, Robbie.

745
01:01:47,246 --> 01:01:48,788
Robbie!

746
01:02:13,564 --> 01:02:16,065
- Robbie. Robbie.
- Robbie.

747
01:02:16,150 --> 01:02:18,151
Robbie!

748
01:02:21,822 --> 01:02:24,073
- Robbie.
- Come on.

749
01:02:24,158 --> 01:02:26,576
Here. Grab my hand.

750
01:02:26,660 --> 01:02:28,536
Here. Hold on.

751
01:02:28,621 --> 01:02:30,913
I got you. Hold on.

752
01:02:30,998 --> 01:02:32,832
Take my hand.

753
01:02:32,916 --> 01:02:35,084
Take it. Take my hand.

754
01:02:35,169 --> 01:02:36,586
Here!

755
01:02:57,024 --> 01:02:59,525
Oh, my God.

756
01:03:18,379 --> 01:03:19,379
Robbie!

757
01:04:03,716 --> 01:04:05,675
Swim. Swim this way.

758
01:04:12,766 --> 01:04:15,560
- Robbie!
- Robbie!

759
01:04:59,146 --> 01:05:02,273
- Help me. Help me with her.
- Here, Rach.

760
01:05:05,110 --> 01:05:07,653
Don't stop. Don't stop.

761
01:05:07,988 --> 01:05:09,655
Don't stop.

762
01:05:26,632 --> 01:05:28,591
Oh, my God.

763
01:06:31,446 --> 01:06:33,114
Robbie, slow down.

764
01:06:43,417 --> 01:06:44,834
Robbie, slow down.

765
01:06:59,016 --> 01:07:01,893
- Robbie.
- We gotta stay together, Robbie.

766
01:07:03,979 --> 01:07:05,563
Robbie?

767
01:07:05,647 --> 01:07:07,148
Stay together.

768
01:07:07,232 --> 01:07:08,816
Robbie!

769
01:07:12,154 --> 01:07:14,322
Get back here!

770
01:07:18,827 --> 01:07:20,411
Robbie!

771
01:07:20,495 --> 01:07:23,664
No, Robbie! Come back!

772
01:07:31,465 --> 01:07:33,090
Robbie.

773
01:07:33,175 --> 01:07:35,134
Don't move. Don't move.

774
01:07:35,218 --> 01:07:38,137
Now, for God's sake, stay right here.
I'm coming right back.

775
01:07:38,221 --> 01:07:40,056
- Robbie!
- Stop those people.

776
01:07:40,140 --> 01:07:42,141
- Turn around. Turn around.
- Robbie.

777
01:07:43,268 --> 01:07:44,560
Robbie.

778
01:07:44,645 --> 01:07:45,937
Robbie.

779
01:07:46,229 --> 01:07:47,355
What the hell?

780
01:07:47,439 --> 01:07:49,482
Why are you doing this?

781
01:07:52,945 --> 01:07:56,364
Pull back.
Five hundred metres to my 10 o'clock.

782
01:07:58,408 --> 01:08:00,534
Jekyll, no effect on target. No effect.

783
01:08:00,619 --> 01:08:02,078
Roger. No effect.

784
01:08:02,162 --> 01:08:04,872
Our mission, Lieutenant,
is to delay their advance

785
01:08:04,957 --> 01:08:08,292
till those refugees get to safety.
Now, keep firing.

786
01:08:10,003 --> 01:08:12,880
You've gotta listen. Turn around!
I want you to listen to me.

787
01:08:15,842 --> 01:08:17,093
Listen to me.

788
01:08:17,177 --> 01:08:18,636
Go back down the hill.

789
01:08:18,720 --> 01:08:21,013
All of you, just turn around.

790
01:08:33,193 --> 01:08:35,611
- Don't do this. I know you wanna fight.
- I wanna be here.

791
01:08:35,696 --> 01:08:37,530
- I need to see this.
- I know it seems like you have to,

792
01:08:37,614 --> 01:08:40,700
- but you don't. You don't.
- Please, let me go.

793
01:08:40,784 --> 01:08:43,202
Okay. Wait, wait, wait.

794
01:08:43,286 --> 01:08:45,287
What are you doing here all by yourself?

795
01:08:45,372 --> 01:08:46,872
Look, sweetie,
you gotta come with us, please.

796
01:08:46,957 --> 01:08:48,958
No. My dad's getting my brother.
I have to stay here.

797
01:08:49,042 --> 01:08:50,251
- You can't stay here.
- We gotta go.

798
01:08:50,335 --> 01:08:51,961
- I'm not gonna leave her alone.
- Leave.

799
01:08:52,045 --> 01:08:54,380
I'm not letting you do this.
You can hate me.

800
01:08:54,464 --> 01:08:56,340
- You can hate me. But I love you.
- Let me go. Please.

801
01:08:56,425 --> 01:08:58,175
- Let me go. Dad.
- I'm not letting you do this.

802
01:08:58,260 --> 01:09:00,886
I can't. No. Please. Please don't pull me.

803
01:09:00,971 --> 01:09:03,472
It's gonna be okay. You need
to come with us. It is not safe...

804
01:09:03,557 --> 01:09:05,683
Please, let me stay here. Please.
I can't go with you.

805
01:09:05,767 --> 01:09:07,309
- My dad's right there.
- Please, come.

806
01:09:07,394 --> 01:09:09,311
- Please, my dad's right there.
- Will you just listen to me?

807
01:09:09,396 --> 01:09:12,189
I need to be here. I want to see this.

808
01:09:12,274 --> 01:09:14,775
Wait. Wait. Just stay for Rachel.
Stay for your sister.

809
01:09:14,860 --> 01:09:18,404
Please, let me go.
You need to let me go.

810
01:09:21,742 --> 01:09:23,075
All right. Okay. All right.
You're coming with us.

811
01:09:23,160 --> 01:09:24,326
- We gotta go! Now!
- Dad.

812
01:09:24,411 --> 01:09:26,328
- We're going now.
- No, no, you don't understand.

813
01:09:26,413 --> 01:09:27,872
Dad!

814
01:09:31,793 --> 01:09:33,210
Dad!

815
01:09:34,254 --> 01:09:36,213
Dad!

816
01:09:41,428 --> 01:09:44,346
Let me go! Dad!

817
01:09:46,266 --> 01:09:49,810
Guide on. Guide on. Black Six.
Attack. Attack. Attack.

818
01:09:52,064 --> 01:09:53,773
Stop.

819
01:09:53,857 --> 01:09:57,026
- That's my dad.
- I'm her father. I'm her father.

820
01:09:57,110 --> 01:09:58,861
- We're so sorry.
- We thought she was alone.

821
01:09:58,945 --> 01:10:01,781
- She was standing by the tree...
- She's fine. Let's go! Let's go!

822
01:10:05,952 --> 01:10:07,286
Robbie.

823
01:10:17,464 --> 01:10:19,924
Robbie!

824
01:10:37,901 --> 01:10:39,443
Over here.

825
01:10:39,528 --> 01:10:40,986
Over here!

826
01:10:44,616 --> 01:10:46,325
Hurry.

827
01:11:05,929 --> 01:11:07,555
Are you all right?

828
01:11:07,931 --> 01:11:09,348
Hey.

829
01:11:11,560 --> 01:11:13,352
What about you, huh?

830
01:11:27,200 --> 01:11:29,034
There you go.

831
01:11:30,579 --> 01:11:32,580
Is that comfortable?

832
01:11:34,541 --> 01:11:37,126
I need you to close your eyes
now, okay?

833
01:11:37,210 --> 01:11:39,044
You need some sleep.

834
01:11:41,423 --> 01:11:42,923
Dad?

835
01:11:43,008 --> 01:11:44,717
He's gonna meet us.

836
01:11:45,927 --> 01:11:48,137
Hey. Robbie's gonna meet us, Rach.

837
01:11:48,221 --> 01:11:50,681
In Boston, at your grandma's.

838
01:11:50,765 --> 01:11:53,934
What do you think
Mom's doing right this minute?

839
01:11:54,019 --> 01:11:55,519
Mom?

840
01:11:56,855 --> 01:11:58,939
Boston. She's waiting.

841
01:11:59,357 --> 01:12:02,860
And I know she's not sleeping,
because she is so worried about you.

842
01:12:02,944 --> 01:12:06,322
And she's in Grandma's kitchen,
and she's...

843
01:12:08,074 --> 01:12:11,076
She's making that awful tea she makes.

844
01:12:11,161 --> 01:12:13,037
And they're all just...

845
01:12:13,705 --> 01:12:17,082
They're all just counting the minutes
until they see you again.

846
01:12:19,252 --> 01:12:22,213
What is this? What is this?

847
01:12:22,839 --> 01:12:25,507
- I won.
- You won?

848
01:12:25,592 --> 01:12:27,885
The walk, trot and canter.

849
01:12:28,053 --> 01:12:30,012
Third place.

850
01:12:38,271 --> 01:12:41,065
<i>Sing me Lullaby and Goodnight.</i>

851
01:12:45,111 --> 01:12:47,112
I don't know that one.

852
01:12:48,114 --> 01:12:50,199
<i>Sing me Hushabye Mountain.</i>

853
01:12:53,745 --> 01:12:57,206
I'm sorry, Rach. I don't...
I don't know that one either.

854
01:13:18,311 --> 01:13:21,772
<i>I'm not bragging, babe
So don't put me down</i>

855
01:13:22,357 --> 01:13:25,526
<i>'Cause I got the fastest
Set of wheels in town</i>

856
01:13:25,694 --> 01:13:28,821
<i>Something comes up to me
They don't even try</i>

857
01:13:30,490 --> 01:13:33,993
<i>'Cause if I had a set of wings
Man, you know she could fly</i>

858
01:13:34,286 --> 01:13:36,829
<i>She's my little deuce coupe</i>

859
01:13:37,789 --> 01:13:40,165
<i>You don't know what I got</i>

860
01:13:41,334 --> 01:13:43,752
<i>Just my little deuce coupe</i>

861
01:13:46,256 --> 01:13:48,507
<i>You don't know what I got</i>

862
01:13:56,766 --> 01:13:58,517
Peach schnapps.

863
01:13:58,601 --> 01:14:02,187
Disgusting, I know it.
Found a whole case of this shit.

864
01:14:09,362 --> 01:14:11,071
Thank you.

865
01:14:16,202 --> 01:14:18,329
I'm sorry about your son.

866
01:14:18,413 --> 01:14:19,997
We got separated. He's...

867
01:14:20,081 --> 01:14:23,208
He's gonna meet us in Boston.

868
01:14:30,050 --> 01:14:31,216
Did you...

869
01:14:33,470 --> 01:14:35,721
Did you lose anybody?

870
01:14:37,724 --> 01:14:39,558
All of them.

871
01:14:42,354 --> 01:14:44,897
Harlan Ogilvy.

872
01:14:45,857 --> 01:14:47,232
Ray Ferrier.

873
01:14:47,317 --> 01:14:48,984
I got water.

874
01:14:50,362 --> 01:14:52,571
Food enough for weeks.

875
01:14:53,406 --> 01:14:56,158
You're welcome to stay. Both of you.

876
01:14:56,326 --> 01:14:58,035
I'm sorry.

877
01:14:59,079 --> 01:15:01,121
I'm gonna get some sleep.

878
01:15:02,874 --> 01:15:07,836
Those machines,
those Tripods they got,

879
01:15:09,923 --> 01:15:11,882
they buried them.

880
01:15:12,884 --> 01:15:14,676
Right under our feet.

881
01:15:16,096 --> 01:15:18,180
Since before there...

882
01:15:18,473 --> 01:15:20,766
There were even people here.

883
01:15:21,351 --> 01:15:24,436
They've been planning this
for a million years.

884
01:15:26,231 --> 01:15:29,274
- We're beat to shit.
- Please.

885
01:15:29,359 --> 01:15:31,652
- My daughter...
- Think about it.

886
01:15:34,739 --> 01:15:38,242
They defeated the greatest power
in the world in a couple days.

887
01:15:38,326 --> 01:15:40,536
Walked right over us.

888
01:15:40,620 --> 01:15:43,831
And these are only the first.
They'll keep coming.

889
01:15:44,999 --> 01:15:46,166
This is not a war

890
01:15:46,251 --> 01:15:49,503
any more than there's
a war between men and maggots.

891
01:15:49,963 --> 01:15:51,964
This is an extermination.

892
01:16:02,642 --> 01:16:03,976
You afraid?

893
01:16:06,146 --> 01:16:07,938
Of course I am.

894
01:16:10,608 --> 01:16:12,734
I been around death plenty.

895
01:16:14,112 --> 01:16:15,821
I drive an ambulance in the city...

896
01:16:15,905 --> 01:16:18,365
Drove an ambulance in the city.

897
01:16:18,616 --> 01:16:20,701
That's all over now, huh?

898
01:16:24,080 --> 01:16:26,957
You know the people that make it, Ray?

899
01:16:27,333 --> 01:16:30,752
The ones that don't flatline
before the hospital?

900
01:16:33,173 --> 01:16:35,924
It's the ones that keep their eyes open.

901
01:16:36,759 --> 01:16:39,511
That keep looking at you. Keep thinking.

902
01:16:40,180 --> 01:16:42,598
They're the ones that survive.

903
01:16:44,058 --> 01:16:46,435
We can't lose our heads, Ray.

904
01:16:48,396 --> 01:16:49,688
Running.

905
01:16:50,398 --> 01:16:52,399
That's what'll kill you.

906
01:16:54,027 --> 01:16:56,695
And I'm dead set on living.

907
01:17:02,202 --> 01:17:04,328
Dead set on living...

908
01:17:07,081 --> 01:17:09,208
Thank you for taking us in.

909
01:17:16,424 --> 01:17:18,467
Not gonna be exterminated.

910
01:17:34,359 --> 01:17:37,486
It's okay. Come on.
I wanna show you something.

911
01:17:38,905 --> 01:17:41,823
We're gonna fight them, Ray.
They got to have a weakness.

912
01:17:41,908 --> 01:17:43,575
Come. Take a look.

913
01:17:51,584 --> 01:17:54,920
Somehow they killed a few of these
things in Osaka. That's what I heard.

914
01:17:55,004 --> 01:17:57,756
You telling me the Japanese
can figure it out, but we can't?

915
01:17:57,840 --> 01:17:59,341
We can do this, Ray.

916
01:17:59,425 --> 01:18:01,301
We can do it. We can get them.

917
01:18:01,386 --> 01:18:03,262
We can figure it out.

918
01:18:03,763 --> 01:18:05,597
Stay right there.

919
01:18:25,034 --> 01:18:26,868
I have a daughter.

920
01:18:26,953 --> 01:18:28,370
Why did you bring us here?

921
01:18:28,454 --> 01:18:31,290
To fight them together, Ray.

922
01:18:31,374 --> 01:18:34,876
Now we'll be the ones coming up
from underground.

923
01:18:36,337 --> 01:18:38,422
When the time is right,

924
01:18:38,506 --> 01:18:41,717
take them by surprise,
the way they took us.

925
01:18:41,801 --> 01:18:44,052
Take them by surprise.

926
01:18:45,221 --> 01:18:46,680
We're right under their feet, Ray.

927
01:18:46,764 --> 01:18:49,641
Right here. Under their feet.

928
01:19:38,191 --> 01:19:40,192
You miss your mommy?

929
01:19:40,902 --> 01:19:42,778
I had a little girl.

930
01:19:43,738 --> 01:19:45,197
Nearly your age.

931
01:19:46,366 --> 01:19:50,786
You know, if anything happens
to your daddy, I'll take care of you.

932
01:19:50,870 --> 01:19:52,079
Rachel.

933
01:20:00,380 --> 01:20:04,216
You don't have anything to say to her.
Do you understand?

934
01:20:04,884 --> 01:20:06,635
If you wanna talk to somebody,

935
01:20:06,719 --> 01:20:08,387
if you wanna ask a question,
you ask me.

936
01:20:08,471 --> 01:20:10,972
What exactly is your plan, Ray?

937
01:20:11,057 --> 01:20:13,975
I know what I'm gonna do.
How about you?

938
01:20:14,060 --> 01:20:17,229
You gonna sit here?
Wait for them to come get you?

939
01:20:17,563 --> 01:20:19,398
Is that your plan?

940
01:20:21,067 --> 01:20:23,276
Maybe you want to get caught.

941
01:20:23,611 --> 01:20:27,155
Couple days hiding in a basement
too much for you, I bet.

942
01:20:27,240 --> 01:20:28,782
You'll probably turn yourself right in.

943
01:20:33,079 --> 01:20:34,413
Listen.

944
01:20:35,790 --> 01:20:38,625
- It stopped.
- Maybe you'll be okay.

945
01:20:38,710 --> 01:20:41,586
Maybe you'll get lucky,
and they'll train you as their pet.

946
01:20:41,671 --> 01:20:44,715
You know, feed you,
train you how to do tricks.

947
01:20:44,799 --> 01:20:46,800
Will you shut up and listen?

948
01:22:50,591 --> 01:22:51,967
No.

949
01:27:15,981 --> 01:27:17,774
Give me that.

950
01:28:51,285 --> 01:28:53,077
You and me,

951
01:28:54,288 --> 01:28:57,373
I don't think we're on the same page.

952
01:29:33,869 --> 01:29:36,496
Ray. Ray.

953
01:29:36,664 --> 01:29:39,415
Ray. Ray. Ray!

954
01:29:39,500 --> 01:29:41,042
Ray!

955
01:29:41,293 --> 01:29:44,212
Keep your voice down. Quiet!

956
01:30:25,629 --> 01:30:28,339
Not my blood. Not my blood.

957
01:30:31,302 --> 01:30:33,219
Not my blood.

958
01:30:34,179 --> 01:30:36,264
Not my...

959
01:30:36,598 --> 01:30:38,099
Not

960
01:30:39,184 --> 01:30:40,518
my...

961
01:30:42,730 --> 01:30:44,647
Not my blood.

962
01:30:45,357 --> 01:30:46,733
Not my blood.

963
01:30:46,859 --> 01:30:48,484
Not my blood.

964
01:30:48,569 --> 01:30:50,194
Not my blood.

965
01:30:50,529 --> 01:30:51,946
Not my blood.

966
01:30:52,114 --> 01:30:53,781
- Not my blood.
- Stop it.

967
01:30:53,866 --> 01:30:54,907
- Stop it.
- Not my blood.

968
01:30:54,992 --> 01:30:56,701
- Stop it.
- Not my blood.

969
01:30:56,785 --> 01:30:58,411
You gotta be quiet.

970
01:30:58,495 --> 01:31:00,621
- You want them to hear you?
- They drink us.

971
01:31:00,706 --> 01:31:02,623
- Please, they'll hear you.
- They drink us.

972
01:31:02,708 --> 01:31:05,793
Then they spray us, like fertiliser.

973
01:31:05,878 --> 01:31:07,128
You gotta be quiet.

974
01:31:07,212 --> 01:31:10,048
- Drink us, and...
- They're gonna come back down here.

975
01:31:10,132 --> 01:31:13,301
Then they spit us out all over
the goddamn red weeds.

976
01:31:13,385 --> 01:31:15,219
Do you understand
what I'm gonna have to do?

977
01:31:15,346 --> 01:31:17,305
I can't let my daughter die
because of you.

978
01:31:17,389 --> 01:31:19,432
This tunnel will get us to the city.

979
01:31:19,516 --> 01:31:21,184
We'll have our own tunnels there.
Ready-made.

980
01:31:21,268 --> 01:31:22,727
- Stop it.
- Subway. See what I'm saying?

981
01:31:22,811 --> 01:31:24,312
- We can hide a whole army down there.
- Stop it.

982
01:31:24,396 --> 01:31:26,147
We'll go underground.
Sneak attacks at night.

983
01:31:26,231 --> 01:31:29,650
Stop. Stop. You stop it!

984
01:31:29,735 --> 01:31:32,987
We're the resistance, Ray.
They can't occupy this country.

985
01:31:33,072 --> 01:31:34,530
Occupations always fail.

986
01:31:34,615 --> 01:31:36,783
History's taught us that
a thousand times.

987
01:31:36,867 --> 01:31:39,077
This is our land.

988
01:31:39,161 --> 01:31:42,622
We eat it, we breathe it,
only we can live on it.

989
01:31:42,706 --> 01:31:45,500
They can't survive here, Ray.
They weren't built for it.

990
01:31:46,251 --> 01:31:49,379
- They're gonna kill you, brother, not me!
- What are you doing?

991
01:31:49,463 --> 01:31:51,381
- Not my blood!
- What are you doing, Dad?

992
01:31:51,465 --> 01:31:54,675
Whatever you hear, don't take this off.

993
01:31:54,760 --> 01:31:56,427
- Dad?
- Rach?

994
01:31:56,512 --> 01:31:58,971
- Dad?
- What was that song?

995
01:31:59,056 --> 01:32:02,683
- That lullaby that I didn't know?
- Not my blood!

996
01:32:02,768 --> 01:32:04,852
<i>- Hushabye Mountain?
- Yeah, sing it.</i>

997
01:32:04,937 --> 01:32:07,688
- They can take you!
- Please, Rach, sing it.

998
01:32:07,773 --> 01:32:09,190
They can take you!

999
01:32:09,274 --> 01:32:10,775
<i>A gentle breeze</i>

1000
01:32:10,859 --> 01:32:13,486
- Your daughter! Not me!
- Don't stop.

1001
01:32:13,570 --> 01:32:15,488
<i>On Hushabye Mountain</i>

1002
01:32:15,572 --> 01:32:17,031
- They're gonna kill you!
- That's my girl.

1003
01:32:17,116 --> 01:32:21,786
<i>Softly blows over Lullaby Bay</i>

1004
01:32:22,746 --> 01:32:23,996
Forget it! Tunnel!

1005
01:32:24,081 --> 01:32:27,083
<i>It fills the sails</i>

1006
01:32:27,709 --> 01:32:30,378
<i>Of boats that are waiting</i>

1007
01:32:32,047 --> 01:32:36,968
<i>Waiting to sail your worries away</i>

1008
01:32:38,679 --> 01:32:42,265
<i>So close your eyes</i>

1009
01:32:42,933 --> 01:32:46,561
<i>On Hushabye Mountain</i>

1010
01:32:46,645 --> 01:32:51,482
<i>Wave goodbye to cares of the day</i>

1011
01:32:52,192 --> 01:32:57,405
<i>And watch your boat
From Hushabye Mountain</i>

1012
01:32:57,906 --> 01:33:03,661
<i>Sail far away
From Lullaby Bay</i>

1013
01:34:56,066 --> 01:34:57,650
Rachel?

1014
01:34:58,110 --> 01:34:59,777
Rachel?

1015
01:35:00,445 --> 01:35:02,405
Oh, my God, no.

1016
01:35:04,157 --> 01:35:06,826
Rachel? Rachel?

1017
01:35:07,578 --> 01:35:09,120
Rachel? Rachel?

1018
01:35:20,382 --> 01:35:22,967
Rachel? Make some noise, baby.

1019
01:35:23,135 --> 01:35:24,427
Rachel?

1020
01:35:25,971 --> 01:35:27,805
Rachel?

1021
01:35:32,227 --> 01:35:34,979
Rachel? Just talk to me, baby. Come on.

1022
01:35:38,734 --> 01:35:40,735
Rachel?

1023
01:35:43,447 --> 01:35:45,573
Rachel?

1024
01:35:59,212 --> 01:36:01,172
Rachel!

1025
01:36:01,340 --> 01:36:03,174
Rachel!

1026
01:37:09,950 --> 01:37:12,827
No, no, no! No!

1027
01:37:44,359 --> 01:37:46,402
Hey!

1028
01:38:25,317 --> 01:38:27,401
Help!

1029
01:38:29,529 --> 01:38:32,406
What is happening?

1030
01:38:34,868 --> 01:38:35,993
Rachel!

1031
01:39:07,859 --> 01:39:09,777
Rachel.

1032
01:39:09,861 --> 01:39:12,488
Rachel. Rachel.

1033
01:39:13,490 --> 01:39:15,449
Rachel.

1034
01:39:16,660 --> 01:39:18,619
Rachel.

1035
01:39:19,454 --> 01:39:21,288
Rachel.

1036
01:39:22,165 --> 01:39:23,374
Dad.

1037
01:39:50,527 --> 01:39:53,445
No! No!

1038
01:39:53,530 --> 01:39:56,115
- Pull me! Pull me!
- No!

1039
01:40:02,622 --> 01:40:05,332
Pull! Pull!

1040
01:40:05,417 --> 01:40:08,043
- Pull me.
- Come on, pull!

1041
01:40:11,172 --> 01:40:13,591
- Dad!
- One, two, three...

1042
01:40:13,675 --> 01:40:15,384
- We got him!
- We got you.

1043
01:40:15,468 --> 01:40:17,052
Keep pulling!

1044
01:40:24,561 --> 01:40:27,187
Everybody down!

1045
01:41:19,407 --> 01:41:21,325
Keep it moving, folks.

1046
01:41:23,870 --> 01:41:26,288
Keep going, sir. Keep moving.

1047
01:41:26,623 --> 01:41:29,166
- Oh, God.
- I don't know what's going on.

1048
01:41:30,961 --> 01:41:32,962
Hold Grandma's hand.

1049
01:41:35,090 --> 01:41:38,550
Let's go, folks. Keep moving forward.

1050
01:41:48,645 --> 01:41:50,437
Put that down.

1051
01:41:52,899 --> 01:41:55,776
Right this way, ma'am.
Right this way. Thank you.

1052
01:42:03,952 --> 01:42:06,912
To the left, there, ma'am,
just to your left. Thank you.

1053
01:42:09,040 --> 01:42:11,166
What happened to it?

1054
01:42:15,046 --> 01:42:16,630
It's dying.

1055
01:42:19,092 --> 01:42:20,801
Keep moving forward.

1056
01:42:31,521 --> 01:42:33,063
Keep moving. It's all right.

1057
01:42:33,148 --> 01:42:34,732
You can pass on through. Move along.

1058
01:42:34,816 --> 01:42:35,899
- What happened here?
- I don't know.

1059
01:42:35,984 --> 01:42:37,985
Something's happening to them.
Please, keep moving.

1060
01:42:38,069 --> 01:42:39,611
- Let's go, move out.
- Let's go, people.

1061
01:42:40,113 --> 01:42:43,240
- Something's happening to them.
- Go. Go, just keep moving, sir.

1062
01:42:43,366 --> 01:42:44,408
Let's go, sir. Let's go.

1063
01:42:44,492 --> 01:42:45,951
Do not stop. Keep moving. Keep moving.

1064
01:42:46,036 --> 01:42:47,369
Excuse me. Excuse me.
What's happened here?

1065
01:42:47,454 --> 01:42:49,997
- Did you guys take it down?
- No, sir, it was behaving erratically,

1066
01:42:50,081 --> 01:42:52,791
walking in circles, then it went down
on its own about an hour ago.

1067
01:42:52,876 --> 01:42:56,003
Now, please, let's go. Let's go.
Keep moving. Come on. Don't stop.

1068
01:42:56,087 --> 01:42:58,172
Do not stop! Let's go! Thank you!

1069
01:42:59,674 --> 01:43:01,592
How is it dead all by itself?

1070
01:43:01,760 --> 01:43:04,386
- Rachel, I'm not sure.
- Coming through.

1071
01:43:04,471 --> 01:43:07,556
Coming through. Make a hole.
Coming through.

1072
01:43:27,619 --> 01:43:29,495
Calm down.
Calm down and get in the tunnel.

1073
01:43:29,579 --> 01:43:31,163
Calm down and get in the tunnel.
Calm down.

1074
01:43:31,247 --> 01:43:33,123
Calm down and get in the tunnel.

1075
01:43:44,969 --> 01:43:48,138
Everybody, calm down.
Get in the tunnel.

1076
01:43:48,223 --> 01:43:51,141
Everybody, on the other side
of the tracks!

1077
01:43:54,646 --> 01:43:55,938
Look at the birds!

1078
01:43:56,022 --> 01:43:57,564
I can't hear you!

1079
01:43:57,649 --> 01:44:00,484
Look at the goddamn birds!

1080
01:44:03,488 --> 01:44:05,697
- No shield!
- I can't hear!

1081
01:44:05,782 --> 01:44:07,616
No shield!

1082
01:44:11,621 --> 01:44:13,997
The Javelin's the key!

1083
01:44:14,082 --> 01:44:16,875
Load the Gustav!
It's gonna be a tough kill!

1084
01:44:17,043 --> 01:44:18,585
Let's go!

1085
01:44:20,421 --> 01:44:21,588
It's safer in here.

1086
01:44:21,673 --> 01:44:23,632
Let's go, let's go, let's go!

1087
01:44:23,716 --> 01:44:25,342
Bring out the Javelin!

1088
01:44:34,144 --> 01:44:36,478
Clear! Go from behind! Clear!

1089
01:44:45,530 --> 01:44:48,115
- Let me know when you're tracking!
- Tracking!

1090
01:44:48,199 --> 01:44:49,741
- You got a lock?
- I got a lock!

1091
01:44:49,826 --> 01:44:51,535
Fire the Javelin!

1092
01:44:58,251 --> 01:45:00,627
- I got a lock!
- Fire the Javelin!

1093
01:45:03,798 --> 01:45:05,257
Fire!

1094
01:45:19,856 --> 01:45:21,648
It's okay.

1095
01:45:22,817 --> 01:45:24,735
I love you.

1096
01:45:24,903 --> 01:45:27,237
- It's okay. You're gonna be okay.
- Let's go!

1097
01:45:28,740 --> 01:45:31,158
Keep those civilians out of there.

1098
01:45:31,242 --> 01:45:35,078
Back. Stay back!
Come on, folks, back up!

1099
01:45:39,918 --> 01:45:43,337
Come on, guys, get on the line.
Get up there now.

1100
01:45:43,421 --> 01:45:46,340
- Stay back. Stay right here, huh?
- Hold on right there.

1101
01:45:52,597 --> 01:45:55,390
- It's opening.
- It's opening. Keep them back.

1102
01:46:34,681 --> 01:46:36,265
Clear!

1103
01:46:36,349 --> 01:46:39,768
No, keep them back. Keep them back.
Come on, stay back.

1104
01:47:15,346 --> 01:47:16,847
Mom!

1105
01:47:44,083 --> 01:47:46,001
Thank you.

1106
01:48:09,400 --> 01:48:11,151
- Robbie?
- Robbie?

1107
01:48:17,658 --> 01:48:19,201
Hi, Dad.

1108
01:48:20,203 --> 01:48:21,912
Hi, Dad.

1109
01:48:22,622 --> 01:48:24,331
Hi, Dad.

1110
01:48:58,658 --> 01:49:01,034
<i>From the moment the invaders arrived,</i>

1111
01:49:01,119 --> 01:49:04,704
<i>breathed our air, ate and drank,</i>

1112
01:49:04,789 --> 01:49:06,456
<i>they were doomed.</i>

1113
01:49:07,500 --> 01:49:10,710
<i>They were undone, destroyed,</i>

1114
01:49:10,795 --> 01:49:14,089
<i>after all of man's weapons
and devices had failed,</i>

1115
01:49:14,382 --> 01:49:19,386
<i>by the tiniest creatures that God
in his wisdom put upon this Earth.</i>

1116
01:49:20,388 --> 01:49:24,182
<i>By the toll of a billion deaths,
man had earned his immunity,</i>

1117
01:49:24,267 --> 01:49:28,854
<i>his right to survive among
this planet's infinite organisms.</i>

1118
01:49:29,939 --> 01:49:33,650
<i>And that right is ours
against all challenges,</i>

1119
01:49:33,985 --> 01:56:05,875
<i>for neither do men live, nor die, in vain.</i>

